# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored -- nothing site-specific
# belongs in a tracked file.
#
#     cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# Both deploy.sh and docker compose read this.

# ---- deploy target (laptop only) -------------------------------------------
# Everything runs on one host: eg4poll, mosquitto, influxdb, and nginx are
# all services in the same docker-compose.yml. Devices, site coordinates,
# and everything else that changes based on what hardware is plugged in are
# configured through the web UI (the Config tab), not here -- see README.
REPO=$HOME/dockers/eg4_poller
POLLER_HOST=poller.example.lan
POLLER_DIR=$HOME/dockers/eg4_poller

# ---- MQTT --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set for the poller account. It's purely internal -- app/poller.py
# talking to this stack's own bundled mosquitto -- never exposed to a
# browser, so there's nothing for a human to type. mosquitto/init-passwd.sh
# generates its password on first boot and shares it with eg4poll only via
# a Docker volume, the same pattern influx/entrypoint.sh uses for the
# InfluxDB admin token.
#
# Password for the ONE account that can write inverter commands, used only
# by solar_settings.html (see mosquitto/acl's `settings` user). Deliberately
# not meant to be a real secret -- its whole job is to stop an accidental or
# scripted publish from the anonymous/read path from ever being mistaken
# for a real command, not to keep out a determined LAN attacker (the ACL is
# what scopes it). Fine to leave as-is; change it here if you want to.
#
# solar_dash.html and config.html need no account at all -- they only read,
# and mosquitto/acl grants anonymous read on energy/# directly. Same for any
# external consumer you wire up yourself (Home Assistant, a NAS recording
# pipeline, another Node-RED instance -- out of scope for this image, see
# README): no credentials needed for reads.
SETTINGS_MQTT_PASS=changeme

# ---- InfluxDB ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set here. Username, password, org, bucket, and the admin token
# are all generated inside the influxdb container on first boot and never
# leave it as plaintext -- see influx/entrypoint.sh. The admin token is
# shared with eg4poll and influx-init only via a Docker volume, not .env.
# 6-month retention (see docker-compose.yml) is the dashboard's history
# window, not a permanent record -- that's whatever you subscribe,
# externally, yourself, to this broker's anonymous read access.

# getent group dialout
DIALOUT_GID=20

# ---- container image (eg4poll only -- the rest build/pull their own) -------
IMAGE=youruser/eg4poll:runtime
